// "Regenerate" = register a one-shot floating replacement shield
// ([CR#614.8,701.19a]): the next time the target would be destroyed this
// turn, instead remove all damage marked on it, tap it, and remove it
// from combat. The shield expires at end of turn if unused ([CR#614.3]).
//
// Usage: Regenerate(target) — e.g. Regenerate(This); Regenerate(It).
// Template: "regenerate ${0}" (matches CR wording, [CR#701.19])
//
// The param is a `Reference` (the permanent to regenerate — `This` or a bound
// `Target`). It is bound by an enclosing `With(TheRef(…))` as the singular
// `That`; the shield freezes THAT resolved binding at creation (an LKI
// snapshot of the protected permanent's identity — `CreateReplacement` no
// longer carries an authored `subject:` field). The watch and the heal/tap
// body refer to that captured permanent as `EventObject` — so `This` is free
// to keep meaning the source ability (it never moves), and the shield works
// for "regenerate target creature" (source ≠ subject), not just self.
//
// The `would` watches the bare-verb `Destroy(…)` pattern twin — the
// present-tense, replaceable destruction keyword-action INTENT ([CR#701.8b]:
// the effect destroy or the lethal-damage SBA, both perform the Destroy
// keyword action). Replacing it here (cant→replace→apply, [CR#614]) means the
// Battlefield → Graveyard move its apply would commit never happens; the
// heal/tap runs instead. `Ref(EventObject)` is the captured subject the shield
// remembers.
(
    name: "Regenerate",
    template: "regenerate ${0}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Reference],
    body: With(
        binder: TheRef(Param(0)),
        body: CreateReplacement(
            replacement: Instead(
                would: Destroy(Ref(EventObject)),
                instead: Sequentially([
                    RemoveDamage(EventObject),
                    Tap(EventObject),
                ]),
            ),
            duration: FixedUntil(EndOfTurn),
            one_shot: true,
        ),
    ),
)
